# paths.env: machine-local config. GITIGNORED; bootstrap.sh copies this file to
# ~/.claude/state/paths.env, then `organism-setup.py` fills it in for you (it detects
# your vault and repos and writes the values, you rarely edit this by hand).
#
# Format: KEY="value", one per line, no trailing comments on assignment lines
# (three different readers parse this file: shell, Python, and guard-publish.js).
# $HOME expands everywhere. Every key is optional: a missing key falls back to a
# default or turns its feature off; nothing crashes.

# ── the vault (your Obsidian notes) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Root of the vault. Session notes and the doc check write here. Without it,
# session notes are off.
# CLAUDE_VAULT_ROOT="$HOME/vault"
# Where session notes land (one note per session + latest.md). Default: the vault's
# _claude-live folder. Set it to "" to turn session notes off.
# CLAUDE_OBSIDIAN_MIRROR_DIR="$HOME/vault/_claude-live"
# Folders whose sessions are never copied into the notes, space-separated absolute
# paths (single-quote one that contains a space). An empty .organism-no-notes file in
# a project folder does the same for that project.
# CLAUDE_NOTES_EXCLUDE="$HOME/clients"
# Folder the doc check (experimental, optional) keeps its pages in.
# CLAUDE_VAULT_WIKI="$HOME/vault/wiki"
# The vault's own decision records, if it keeps any (/handoff run in the vault
# writes them). deploy.sh shows them in this repo as the gitignored docs/vault-adr.
# CLAUDE_VAULT_ADR_DIR="$HOME/vault/docs/adr"

# ── your code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base directory of your git repos; setup looks here for the doc check's repos.
# CLAUDE_CODE_ROOT="$HOME/dev"

# ── the publish guard ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A markdown page listing terms that must never leave this machine in a push or
# deploy (project codenames, unreleased names). See guard-publish.spec.md.
# GUARD_PUBLISH_DENYLIST="$HOME/vault/Confidential Terms.md"

# ── scheduled jobs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For AI jobs you add yourself (agents.local): one model for all of them.
# CLAUDE_LLM_MODEL="claude-opus-5"
# Extra log directories for the weekly log janitor, space-separated.
# CLAUDE_ROTATE_EXTRA_DIRS=""

# ── tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Directory holding the `claude` CLI, if a job you add calls it and it isn't on PATH.
# CLAUDE_BIN_DIR=""
# Repos the doc check leaves out when setup generates its pairings (space-separated,
# relative to CLAUDE_CODE_ROOT). Everything discovered is checked unless listed here.
# CLAUDE_RECONCILE_EXCLUDE=""
